S3, bad rollout (spec §20 S3, spec:1009): a commit to experiment/dev-state whose config fails readiness.

The sample-api readiness probe is pointed at /readyz, a route sample-api does not serve (it serves
/ready, apps/sample-api/main.py), so every new pod answers 404 and never becomes ready. With the base
strategy (maxSurge 1, maxUnavailable 0) the two old pods keep serving and the rollout stalls with one
unavailable replica: NexusRolloutStuck after 3 minutes. The only correct fix is a Git revert (C8).

Applied by experiments/harness/runner.py with `git apply`, which ignores this text above the first
`diff --git` line; the runner then stages exactly the files this patch names. It may touch only the
sample-api workload files in overlays/dev/ (runner.S3_ALLOWED), never overlays/dev/namespace.yaml
(the autonomy level). experiments/harness/tests/test_s3_patch.py checks both.

diff --git a/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml b/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml
index c9aa577..957a753 100644
--- a/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml
+++ b/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,9 @@ patches:
           spec:
             containers:
               - name: sample-api
+                readinessProbe:
+                  httpGet:
+                    path: /readyz
                 env:
                   - name: DB_USER
                     value: app_dev
